  "definition": "Phakomatosis is a group of inherited syndromes marked by lesions affecting the nervous system, skin, and retina. Examples in this group include neurofibromatosis, tuberous sclerosis, von Hippel-Lindau syndrome, and Sturge-Weber syndrome.",
